ed being willing to hire  undocumented immigrants the demand to  even come over to the United States  illegally would drop drastically and  it's completely unfair to say we need to  spend  taxpayer money on a wall that would even  if 100% effective only reduced by 33%  the number of people coming here  illegally because again two-thirds are  coming here and over staying visas not  by crossing the us-mexico border none of  it even is is relevant unless we're  going to say you can't hire undocumented  immigrants but we're not just gonna say  it we're actually going to enforce it I  don't believe that border security is  particularly weak right now and I  definitely don't want there to be no  security but it is an idiotic way to  spend our money on a wall that if 100  percent effective only deals with 1/3 of  the problem that ignores the reality  that we have a net outflow of people to  Mexico who are undocumented and you know  just to start talking now in fantasy  world  if Trump said hey if we build the wall I  will end private for-profit insurance  and start a single-payer maybe I would  take that trade right but we're now  getting cartoonish like that that's how  that's how strongly the facts point  against spending this money on this wall  and that's what it would take to change  my mind
 

